# Input
```
-- dbmate sends a section to Postgres as one query, which runs in a transaction block if it has
-- more than one statement, also after a COMMIT.
-- section: up transaction:false
-- expect_lint/banConcurrentIndexCreationInTransaction
CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY users_email_idx ON users (email);
BEGIN;
COMMIT;
-- expect_lint/banConcurrentIndexCreationInTransaction
CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY users_name_idx ON users (name);

```

# Diagnostics
lint/banConcurrentIndexCreationInTransaction ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY cannot run inside a transaction block.
  
  i Run CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY outside of a transaction block, e.g. in a migration of its own that runs without a transaction.
  
  i The migration tool sends the statements to Postgres as one query, and Postgres runs a query with more than one statement in a transaction block. Put the statement in a section of its own.
  


